Third-party software
--------------------

DBeast depends on open source Rust crates listed in Cargo.lock, each
distributed under its own license. Nearly all use permissive licenses (MIT,
Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0, BSL-1.0, CC0-1.0 and similar).
The following dependencies use other licenses and are used unmodified:

- option-ext (MPL-2.0), through directories. Source:
  https://github.com/soc/option-ext
- self_cell (Apache-2.0 OR GPL-2.0-only), used under Apache-2.0.
- webpki-roots (CDLA-Permissive-2.0), the Mozilla root certificate bundle
  used by ureq for map tile downloads.

The bundled SQLite (through rusqlite) is in the public domain.
